    int a = rand() % (1000 - 999 + 1) + 999;
    int b = rand() % (1000 - 999 + 1) + 999;
    int c = rand() % (1000 - 999 + 1) + 999;

    // Print the three integers
    printf("a : %d\n", a);
    printf("b : %d\n", b);
    printf("c : %d\n", c);

    // Add the three integers and print the result
    int sum = a + b + c;
    printf("sum: %d\n", sum);

    // Add the three integers using a long long and print the result
    long long sum2 = (long long)a + (long long)b + (long long)c;
    printf("sum2: %lld\n", sum2);

    return 0;
}
```
This code uses the `rand()` function to generate three random integers between 1000 and 999, inclusive. The `%` operator is used to ensure that the result is an integer. The `srand()` function is used to seed the random number generator with the current time.

